      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 136,
      "outputTokens": 864,
      "costUsd": 0.007844,
      "pronunciationText": "Now use it to add any geometric sequence. S sub n is a, plus a r, plus a r squared, up to a r to the n minus one. Take out the a, and the bracket is exactly the one we just expanded, with r in place of x. So r minus one, times S sub n, is a, times r to the n, minus one. To get S sub n alone, divide by r minus one. That's only allowed if r isn't one, because then we'd be dividing by zero. And if r is one, every term is a, so the sum is just n lots of ay."
    },
