      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 106,
      "outputTokens": 784,
      "costUsd": 0.007109,
      "pronunciationText": "Multiply the top and bottom by minus one, and you get the form in the syllabus: a, times one minus r to the n, all over one minus r. Both forms always give the same value. When r is bigger than one, the r minus one form keeps the top and bottom positive. When r is between minus one and one, the one minus r form does. Some books get S sub n by multiplying it by r and subtracting. That's the same shift and cancel, done row by row."
    },
