      "inputTokens": 77,
      "outputTokens": 593,
      "costUsd": 0.0053755,
      "pronunciationText": "So how much rice is on the whole chessboard? Here ay is one, r is two and n is sixty-four, so the total is two to the sixty-four, minus one. That's about eighteen billion billion grains, which is hundreds of years of the whole world's rice harvest. The last square alone holds more than all the other squares put together."
