      "inputTokens": 131,
      "outputTokens": 951,
      "costUsd": 0.0086245,
      "pronunciationText": "Let's use it. Find the sum from k equals one to six of three times two to the k minus one. The rule gives three, six, twelve, so ay is three and r is two. The counter goes from one to six, so there are six terms. Since r is bigger than one, use the r minus one form. That's three, times two to the six, minus one, over two minus one. Two to the six is sixty-four, so it's three times sixty-three, which is one hundred and eighty-nine. Adding the six terms one by one gives the same total."
    },
