      "pronunciationText": "Signs need care when r is negative. Find the sum of the first six terms of one, minus three, plus nine, minus twenty-seven, and so on. Here ay is one, and r is minus three. Use the one minus r form, with brackets around minus three. Minus three to the six is seven hundred and twenty-nine, because an even power of a negative is positive. So the top is one minus seven hundred and twenty-nine, and the bottom is one plus three, which is four. The sum is minus seven hundred and twenty-eight over four, which is minus one hundred and eighty-two."
    },
