      "costUsd": 0.008603999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "One more, with a ratio less than one. Find the sum of the first eight terms of sixty-four, plus thirty-two, plus sixteen, and so on. Here ay is sixty-four and r is a half. Use the one minus r form: sixty-four, times one minus a half to the eight, over one minus a half. Dividing by a half doubles, so that's one hundred and twenty-eight, times one minus one over two hundred and fifty-six. That's one hundred and twenty-eight, minus a half, so the sum is one hundred and twenty-seven and a half. Notice how close that is to one hundred and twenty-eight."
